<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3487" root="بوأ" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَآءٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَآءَةٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  A <i>libidinous</i> man. (TA in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">باب</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الالف الليّنة</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  The <i>name of the letter</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span>, q. v.;
as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَا</span>: pl. of the former <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَآءَاتٌ</span>; and of the
latter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْوَآءٌ</span>. (TA ubi suprà.) The dim. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُيَيَّةٌ</span>,
meaning <i>A little</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span>: and <i>a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ب</span> <i>faintly pronounced:</i>
[and app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُوَيَّةٌ</span> also, as the medial radical is generally held to be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span>:] and in like manner is formed
the dim. of every similar name of a letter. (Lth,
on the letter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَآء</span>, in TA, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">باب الالف اللينّة</span>.)

